      "sofaID": "_InitialView",
      "mimeType": "text",
      "sofaString": "9002\tPt, Micah Torres, is a 12 year old male with a history of focal segmental glomerulosclerosis referred for Kidney Transplant Psychosocial Assessment.  Information for this assessment was obtained through interviews with the patient and his mother, and review of the medical record.  SW spent 60 minutes of face to face time with patient and family.  Family history: the family reports a prior Department of Child and Family involvement approximately five years ago related to housing instability, which has since been resolved.  The family denies any current involvement with child protective services.  Mental health: Micah's mother reports a history of generalized anxiety, currently managed with outpatient counseling.  Micah himself denies any mental health concerns at this time.  Substance use: the family denies any current or past substance use in the home.  Adherence: the family reports occasional missed doses of Micah's immunosuppressant medication due to a hectic school schedule.  The mother verbalizes a strong understanding of the medication regimen and transplant process.  Assessment and recommendations: the primary psychosocial concern is moderate medication non-adherence related to scheduling conflicts.  The family appears otherwise well supported and engaged in Micah's care.  Recommendations: refer the family to the adherence support program and provide a pill organizer with alarm reminders.  Continue routine psychosocial follow-up at each clinic visit.\n\nPriya Nandakumar, LCSW\nPediatric Transplant Team\n(000) 000-0000"
    }
  }
